    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Great Work Keystone.</strong> You can design a project whose whole is kinder than the sum of its parts.</p><ul><li>Once per strategic arc, you may designate a multi-hex project (fortification belt, canal, transit line, shrine network, etc.) as a <strong>Great Work Keystone Project</strong>.</li><li>While this project is underway and you are actively involved, <strong>hex-level improvements</strong> made as part of it (Loyalty bumps, Darkness reduction, infrastructure upgrades) are slightly more efficient: they may cost 1 fewer OP, grant +1 additional benefit, or resolve one step faster (GM sets the exact expression).</li><li>This feature narratively and mechanically ties several Soul-Smith actions into a single, named piece of the Great Work.</li></ul>",
